{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794389755,"nonce":"u7m4HMPVBQ8j/Zd6DQeBPPnxNig=","message":"Futures no longer wait on this. hxn-future keeps a result in Rust until a Haxe thread takes it, so settling from a native thread touches no runtime: no thread registration, no root, no call into the VM. `hxn.Future.then` delivers on the calling thread's event loop from a Haxe helper thread.\n\nWhat is still open here is a Haxe closure passed into Rust, and with it the questions about a handle that owns a root.","files":null}]}